    "title": "Motorcyclist killed in Waterloo crash on Highway 63, police say - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alex Lawson ,\n12 hours ago A motorcyclist died Wednesday afternoon after a crash on Sergeant Road, also known as Highway 63, near Freedom Lane in Waterloo, officials said.\nAccording to officials, Black Hawk County Consolidated Dispatch received a 911 call about the crash at about 3:47 p.m. July 1, 2026.\nWaterloo police and Waterloo Fire & Rescue responded to the scene. Officers found that the male rider had come off the motorcycle during the crash, officials said.\nThe rider was pronounced dead at the scene.\nOfficials said witness accounts indicated the motorcycle was the only vehicle involved and that the rider was the only person on it.\nIowa News Originally published by Iowa Pulse . For more verified Iowa news and real-time updates, follow Iowa Pulse.\n4",
    "summary": "3 hours ago A motorcyclist died Wednesday afternoon after a crash on Sergeant Road, also known as Highway 63, near Freedom Lane in Waterloo, officials said. According to officials, Black Hawk County Consolidated Dispatch received a 911 call about the crash at about 3:47 p.m. July 1, 2026. Officers found that the male rider had come off the motorcycle during the crash, officials said. The rider was pronounced dead at the scene. Officials said witness accounts indicated the motorcycle was the only vehicle involved and that the rider was the only person on it.",
